    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0caea995-3666-5c91-8c4b-ea6958f81d41",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 9 & 24 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 16\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 9 & 24 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 16\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 16\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y &=8 \\\\ y &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=0$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+3\\left(0\\right)=8\\,\\Rightarrow\\,x=8+0=8.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=8$ and $y=0.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
